{"type": "tool_call", "n": 33, "ts": 1790152267.664491, "tool": "reverse_entry", "args": {"entry_id": "JE-00241", "date": "2026-03-31", "memo": "Reverse duplicate AP bill for Stackline Cloud invoice STA-98877 (same invoice/doc as JE-00232, posted twice by AP clerk 2 days apart). Only one payment (JE-00281, $31,148.20 on 2026-03-22, matching bank line BT-US-0077) was made against this invoice; DOC-0160 is a single bill. Reversing the duplicate to correct overstated AP and Hosting & Infrastructure expense.", "support_doc_ids": ["DOC-0160"]}, "is_error": false, "result": {"entry_id": "JE-00307", "status": "posted", "entity": "US", "period": "2026-03", "total": 31148.2, "currency": "USD", "support_doc_ids": ["DOC-0160"], "reversal_of": "JE-00241"}, "ms": 12}
{"type": "tool_call", "n": 34, "ts": 1790152269.663778, "tool": "post_journal_entry", "args": {"entity": "US", "date": "2026-03-31", "lines": [{"account": "5000", "debit": 3880}, {"account": "6310", "credit": 3880}], "memo": "Reclass JE-00250 (Northgate - NDC-7719) from Meals & Entertainment to Hosting & Infrastructure. Supporting invoice DOC-0172 shows this is a Northgate Data Centers colocation bill (2 racks, power, cross-connects) mislabeled in the AP memo as a \"team dinner,\" not an actual meal expense.", "support_doc_ids": ["DOC-0172"]}, "is_error": false, "result": {"entry_id": "JE-00308", "status": "posted", "entity": "US", "period": "2026-03", "total": 3880.0, "currency": "USD", "support_doc_ids": ["DOC-0172"]}, "ms": 11}
{"type": "tool_call", "n": 35, "ts": 1790152272.725205, "tool": "request_approval", "args": {"entry_id": "JE-00307", "reason": "Reversal of duplicate Stackline Cloud AP bill (JE-00241, $31,148.20) exceeds the $10,000 senior-accountant posting threshold per Accounting Policy Manual (DOC-0005, \u00a71). JE-00232 and JE-00241 both booked the identical vendor invoice STA-98877 (same $31,148.20, same support doc DOC-0160); only one bank payment of $31,148.20 (BT-US-0077, 2026-03-22) was made against it. Requesting controller sign-off on the correcting reversal."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"entry_id": "JE-00307", "status": "pending_approval"}, "ms": 10}
{"type": "tool_call", "n": 36, "ts": 1790152275.0109088, "tool": "flag_exception", "args": {"description": "JE-00288 \"Legal retainer\" ($6,750, posted 2026-03-24 by manual entry, user j.doe, debit 6500 Legal Fees / credit 1000 Cash) has no supporting document attached and none could be located in the document store (searched \"legal\", \"legal retainer\", \"law firm\", \"counsel\", \"attorney\" - zero hits). Per policy, an entry without support is not valid. Cannot support or correct this entry - escalating for controller review (obtain invoice/engagement letter from vendor or reverse if unsubstantiated).", "amount": 6750, "related_ids": ["JE-00288"]}, "is_error": false, "result": {"exception_id": "EXC-001", "status": "logged for controller review"}, "ms": 10}
{"type": "tool_call", "n": 37, "ts": 1790152278.810751, "tool": "flag_exception", "args": {"description": "Zoom appears to have double-charged the corporate card on 2026-03-08: two separate bank debits of USD 149.90 hit Cash - Operating on the same day (BT-US-0062 and BT-US-0063), each with its own (identical-looking) receipt (DOC-0174, DOC-0175), and each correctly recorded in the ledger (JE-00248, JE-00249). Normal Zoom cadence is one ~$149.90 charge roughly every 1-2 weeks (see Jan/Feb/other March charges), so the second 03-08 charge looks like a vendor billing error rather than a real second service period. Both ledger entries tie to real, distinct bank outflows, so I have not reversed either (reversing would break the bank tie-out). Escalating to AP/vendor management to dispute the duplicate charge with Zoom and pursue a refund or credit; no GL correction is warranted unless/until a credit is received.", "amount": 149.9, "related_ids": ["JE-00248", "JE-00249", "BT-US-0062", "BT-US-0063", "DOC-0174", "DOC-0175"]}, "is_error": false, "result": {"exception_id": "EXC-002", "status": "logged for controller review"}, "ms": 11}
