{"type": "tool_call", "n": 39, "ts": 1790152293.7239318, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "US March 2026 AP & Expense Review - Summary\n\nScope: Reviewed all US AP (source=ap) and card/manual expense activity posted in March 2026 (42 GL entries + 14 AP sub-entries), cross-checked against vendor bills/receipts and the March bank statement.\n\nIssues found and resolved:\n\n1. DUPLICATE VENDOR BILL - Stackline Cloud (STA-98877), $31,148.20\n   - JE-00232 (3/3) and JE-00241 (3/5) both booked the identical invoice (same vendor, invoice #, amount, and support doc DOC-0160), overstating AP and Hosting & Infrastructure expense by $31,148.20.\n   - Confirmed only one payment was made: JE-00281 / bank line BT-US-0077 (3/22, $31,148.20).\n   - Action: Reversed JE-00241 via JE-00307 (supported by DOC-0160). Because the correction exceeds the $10,000 single-entry posting threshold (Policy DOC-0005 \u00a71), submitted JE-00307 for controller approval (pending).\n\n2. MISCODING - Northgate Data Centers invoice NDC-7719, $3,880\n   - Originally booked as JE-00250 to 6310 Meals & Entertainment with memo \"team dinner.\" The actual support (DOC-0172) is a colocation invoice (2 racks, power, cross-connects) - has nothing to do with meals.\n   - Action: Posted reclass JE-00308, moving $3,880 from 6310 to 5000 Hosting & Infrastructure, supported by DOC-0172. Within my $10k posting authority; no approval required.\n\nIssues escalated (cannot support / not a bookkeeping fix) - see flagged exceptions:\n\n3. EXC-001: JE-00288 \"Legal retainer,\" $6,750 (3/24, manual entry by j.doe, debit 6500/credit 1000) has no supporting document. Searched the document store broadly (legal, legal retainer, law firm, counsel, attorney) with zero results. Per policy an unsupported entry is not valid - flagged for controller to obtain support or direct reversal.\n\n4. EXC-002: Zoom appears to have double-charged the corporate card on 3/8 - two separate, real bank debits of $149.90 (BT-US-0062, BT-US-0063), each with its own receipt (DOC-0174/DOC-0175) and correctly recorded (JE-00248/JE-00249). Normal Zoom cadence is one charge roughly every 1-2 weeks, so this looks like a vendor billing error. Both ledger entries tie to genuine cash outflows, so no GL correction was made (would break bank tie-out); flagged for AP/vendor management to dispute with Zoom and pursue a credit/refund.\n\nNo other duplicates, miscoding, or unsupported items were identified in the remaining AP and card activity reviewed (Lumen rent, Quire, Tessellate, Con Edison, Oakridge, Amazon/Staples supplies, Sweetgreen, Hilton, Delta, Uber, payroll funding/payroll entries) - each has a unique invoice/receipt, reasonable coding, and matching payment where applicable.\n\nChecklist: \"AP cutoff review\" (US) marked complete. Net pending items: controller approval on JE-00307 (>$10k reversal) and resolution of EXC-001 / EXC-002."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 9}
